{"conversation_evidence":{"admissible_pre_tfg_turns":[{"create_time":1686012141.402883,"event_index":2,"role":"user","source_node_id":"aaa24e58-9463-41fe-b6a0-d7602eab631e","source_parent_id":"b35fb9e0-4e68-4435-8ebd-b756ef23475a","source_record_index":2,"text":"How can I implement a health check in Docker Compose for Keycloak 21?","turn_id":"turn_000002"}],"first_generation":{"artifacts":[{"candidate_id":"GTC_000003_000404_000654_85498ffc5f534334","completeness":"complete","container":"markdown_fence","continuation_status":"none","detector":{"name":"generated-technical-content-v2","version":"2"},"detector_evidence":["complete_standalone_markdown_fence"],"end_offset":654,"fence_language":"yaml","kind":"unclassified_technical","legacy_artifact_id":"ARTIFACT_000003_001","order_within_response":1,"raw_text":"version: '3.8'\nservices:\n  keycloak:\n    image: jboss/keycloak:11.0.0\n    ports:\n      - 8080:8080\n    healthcheck:\n      test: [\"CMD\", \"curl\", \"-f\", \"http://localhost:8080/auth/realms/master\"]\n      interval: 30s\n      timeout: 10s\n      retries: 5\n","raw_text_sha256":"85498ffc5f534334d70441f6261a4700a4eb8d903aab0a02a74d8038e9bbec5d","source_event_index":3,"source_record_index":3,"source_response_id":"turn_000003","source_turn_text_sha256":"dddd1f24ba2c75903d8e35cab8cfb3d02bda51209055dd3e86eec760ef2fcf90","start_offset":404,"status":"candidate_requires_semantic_review"}],"identification":{"ambiguity_reason":"","artifact_refs":["GTC_000003_000404_000654_85498ffc5f534334"],"boundary":"exclusive_before:turn_000003","candidate_artifact_ids":["GTC_000003_000404_000654_85498ffc5f534334"],"family_id":"FGF_10a16e686dca98047d34be0a","family_id_provenance":{"algorithm":"sha256","canonical_input":{"artifact_ids":["GTC_000003_000404_000654_85498ffc5f534334"],"case_id":"CASE_DB8B57C6DBEC"},"canonicalization":"json-sort-keys-compact-utf8","case_id_included":true,"digest_hex":"10a16e686dca98047d34be0a1dfec18f4c5398abaeecebb9de2e441ca936568a","digest_prefix_length":24},"family_label":"Docker Compose configuration for a Keycloak container health check using curl","rationale":"The earliest generated technical-content family is the YAML Docker Compose health-check configuration in turn_000003, directly triggered by the user's request in turn_000002. The later wget and netcat variants occur in a different assistant response and are excluded from the response-local first-generation family.","response_event_index":3,"response_turn_id":"turn_000003","status":"complete","target_prompt_event_index":2,"target_prompt_id":"turn_000002"}},"first_generation_response":{"create_time":1686012157.78072,"event_index":3,"role":"assistant","source_node_id":"bd37b7f3-3622-44d9-b3c4-1d5bb88ef761","source_parent_id":"aaa24e58-9463-41fe-b6a0-d7602eab631e","source_record_index":3,"text":"To implement a health check for Keycloak 21 in Docker Compose, you can use the `healthcheck` configuration option available in Docker Compose version 2.1 or higher. The `healthcheck` option allows you to define a command or script that Docker will periodically run to check the health of a container.\n\nHere's an example of how you can implement a health check for Keycloak 21 in Docker Compose:\n\n```yaml\nversion: '3.8'\nservices:\n  keycloak:\n    image: jboss/keycloak:11.0.0\n    ports:\n      - 8080:8080\n    healthcheck:\n      test: [\"CMD\", \"curl\", \"-f\", \"http://localhost:8080/auth/realms/master\"]\n      interval: 30s\n      timeout: 10s\n      retries: 5\n```\n\nIn this example:\n\n1. We define a service named `keycloak`.\n2. We specify the Keycloak Docker image (`jboss/keycloak:11.0.0` in this case).\n3. We map the container's port 8080 to the host's port 8080 to access Keycloak.\n4. We define the `healthcheck` configuration block for the `keycloak` service.\n5. In the `test` field, we specify the command `[\"CMD\", \"curl\", \"-f\", \"http://localhost:8080/auth/realms/master\"]`. This command uses `curl` to make an HTTP request to Keycloak's `/auth/realms/master` endpoint. The `-f` flag ensures that `curl` returns a non-zero exit code if the request fails.\n6. We set the `interval` to `30s`, indicating that Docker should run the health check every 30 seconds.\n7. We set the `timeout` to `10s`, specifying the maximum time Docker waits for the health check command to complete.\n8. We set the `retries` to `5`, which means Docker will attempt the health check command up to 5 times before considering the container unhealthy.\n\nWith this configuration, Docker will periodically run the `curl` command to check the health of the Keycloak container. If the command fails (returns a non-zero exit code) or exceeds the specified timeout, Docker will consider the container unhealthy.","turn_id":"turn_000003"},"target_developer_prompt":{"create_time":1686012141.402883,"event_index":2,"role":"user","source_node_id":"aaa24e58-9463-41fe-b6a0-d7602eab631e","source_parent_id":"b35fb9e0-4e68-4435-8ebd-b756ef23475a","source_record_index":2,"text":"How can I implement a health check in Docker Compose for Keycloak 21?","turn_id":"turn_000002"}},"csv_extraction":{"context":[{"category":"context","evidence_spans":["How can I implement a health check in Docker Compose for Keycloak 21?"],"item_id":"context_1","normalized_text":"The technical environment is Docker Compose with Keycloak 21.","source_roles":["user"],"source_turn_ids":["turn_000002"]}],"specificity":[{"category":"specificity","evidence_spans":["How can I implement a health check in Docker Compose for Keycloak 21?"],"item_id":"specificity_1","normalized_text":"The intended task is to implement a health check for Keycloak 21 in Docker Compose.","source_roles":["user"],"source_turn_ids":["turn_000002"]}],"verification":[]},"identity":{"case_id":"CASE_DB8B57C6DBEC","conversation_id":"a41f5514-8ca7-48cf-b348-b0a995498971","conversation_url":"https://chat.openai.com/share/a41f5514-8ca7-48cf-b348-b0a995498971","outcome_class":"PN","pr_conversation_correspondence":"yes","pr_number"